--   APSP in $O(n^{2.99791})$: definitions, part 3 of 5
-- statement:
--   Definitions for the formal proof that all-pairs shortest paths can be solved deterministically in time $O(n^{2.99791})$ on a word RAM, part 3 of 5. It imports `APSP299791_Defs2`.
--
--   This part contains the contracts of the Section 4 routines for pruned encodings (Contracts, Memory, SharedP), the contracts of the pruned encoder and the pruned shared stage (Programs.Sec2.PrunedEnc.Contracts), and the parameter choices and limits of Section 4 (Corollary 31, Programs.Sec4.ChoosingParameters).
--
--   Source modules (in this order): `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec4.Theorem30.Query`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec4.Theorem30.Routines`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec2.PrunedEnc.AllBands`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec2.PrunedEnc.SharedStage`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec2.PrunedEnc.Recursion`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec4.Theorem30.Program`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec4.ChoosingParameters.Program`, `ThreeSumApsp.Sec4.Table2.LogBounds`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec5.Corollary39.GraphH.Fill`, `ThreeSumApsp.Programs.Sec5.Corollary40.DataStructureBounds`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.ScanPairs`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.Task`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.Data`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.Loop`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.Host`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.MidHost`, `ThreeSumApsp.AllEdges.RatParams`.
--
--   Across the six parts, the development changes the construction of Alman and Vassilevska Williams in three ways:
--
--   1. *pruned encodings* in the data structure of Theorem 30: only the leaves whose $L$ decimal digits contain at most $m$ nines are computed and stored, since a query reads no other leaf, and the shared stage costs $\sum_{j\le m}\binom Lj9^{L-j}$ per band instead of $10^L$;
--   2. the thin regime $D^{91}\le N^5$ with the parameters $c=22$, $\theta=29/250$;
--   3. an all-edges Exact Triangle host for Theorem 17 that calls its oracle at the middle dimension $\lceil s/g\rceil s$, $s=\lfloor\sqrt D\rfloor$, followed by the chain all-edges Exact Triangle → pairs → (min,+)-product → APSP.
